elta del cuerpo a la cultura popular blanca. Los institucionalizaron las discotecas (el Whisky a Go Go del Sunset Strip, enero de 1964, con chicas bailando en jaulas) y los programas de televisión (Shindig!, Hullabaloo, Where the Action Is). «Land of 1000 Dances», de Chris Kenner (1962), enumeraba los bailes; Cannibal & the Headhunters, del este de Los Ángeles, le añadieron el «na na-ne-na-na» en 1965. En 1966 llegó el Boo-Ga-Loo de Tom and Jerrio, mezcla de Motown, aire latino y gritos a lo James Brown, en la estela de «Let’s Dance» de Chris Montez y «Wooly Bully» de Sam the Sham, el single más vendido de 1965.","color":"#facc15","family":"Soul, Motown, R&B y ska","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/1966/#bailes"}],"aka":[{"id":175801727766171,"type":"genre","name":"Del Twist al Boo-Ga-Loo: bailes y discotecas","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":19,"yt":null,"src":"books"},{"id":259421449681721,"type":"genre","name":"Chuck Brown","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":1,"yt":null,"src":"books"},{"id":123047313255031,"type":"genre","name":"Rare Essence","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":1,"yt":null,"src":"books"},{"id":81888978816476,"type":"genre","name":"Trouble Funk","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":1,"yt":null,"src":"books"},{"id":26434986970232,"type":"genre","name":"E.U.","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":1,"yt":null,"src":"books"}],"rym":[{"id":199315475780166,"name":"RYM Top — R&B — Go-Go","total":32,"url":"https://rateyourmusic.com/charts/top/album/all-time/g:go-go/","items":[{"id":197179871005538,"type":"album","name":"Bustin' Loose","artist":"Chuck Brown & The Soul Searchers","year":1979,"rank":1,"yt":"3vvUO8IQyAQ"},{"id":246632861275142,"type":"album","name":"Salt of the Earth","artist":"The Soul Searchers","year":1974,"rank":2,"yt":"-ODhEvPn88c"},{"id":134148177680530,"type":"album","name":"DMR","artist":"Mix-O-Rap","year":2014,"rank":3,"yt":"QbHYOyw-res"},{"id":117118100142536,"type":"album","name":"Drop the Bomb","artist":"Trouble Funk","year":1982,"r